@startuml 06-sync-outbox
title Geonera Ingestion — 6. Sync: Outbox Worker (SyncTask drain)
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #1B1B1B
skinparam ArrowColor #546E7A
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #1B1B1B
  FontSize 13

  BackgroundColor<<lock>> #EF6C00
  FontColor<<lock>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<lock>> #A34B00

  BackgroundColor<<db>> #1565C0
  FontColor<<db>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<db>> #0B3C78

  BackgroundColor<<r2>> #2E7D32
  FontColor<<r2>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<r2>> #1B5E20

  BackgroundColor<<api>> #AD1457
  FontColor<<api>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<api>> #6A0F38
}

skinparam activityDiamond {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3CD
  BorderColor #C79100
  FontColor #5D4037
}

skinparam legend {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #90A4AE
  FontColor #1B1B1B
  FontSize 12
  EntrySeparatorColor #CFD8DC
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #3E3E3E
}

legend right
  |= Tag |= Meaning |
  |<back:#EF6C00><color:#FFFFFF> lock </color></back>| Advisory-lock / Parent Handler step |
  |<back:#1565C0><color:#FFFFFF> db </color></back>| PostgreSQL transaction (state / outbox) |
  |<back:#2E7D32><color:#FFFFFF> r2 </color></back>| Cloudflare R2 storage I/O |
  |<back:#AD1457><color:#FFFFFF> api </color></back>| External Dukascopy API call |
endlegend

start
:runSyncHandler(ctx, dal);<<lock>>
note right
  Triggered by queue jobs.sync (every 5 minutes).
  Acquires LockIDSync (1004) via Direct Connection.
  Implements the consumer side of the
  **Transactional Outbox Pattern** (see 6.1) —
  guarantees ResolvedTickCount is recomputed
  reliably even across crashes / lost updates.
end note

note right
  ** Reminder — how SyncTask rows get created (publish side, NOT this process): **
  Whenever a TICK row reaches a terminal/demoted state
  (-> CONFIRMED, or CONFIRMED -> BROKEN demotion) inside
  the T-2 / Backfill-Validate workers, an
  "INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (instrument_id, target_date)
  DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status" is executed
  in the SAME DB transaction as the status change —
  this both records the event AND resurrects/ resets
  any existing task for that day back to PENDING.
end note

:processSyncTask(ctx, dal)
via dal.ExecuteInPool (PgBouncer connection);
:**Atomic claim using a CTE**:
"SELECT ... FROM sync_tasks
 WHERE status='PENDING'
 FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED ...
 then UPDATE status='PROCESSED'"
executed as a single statement
(no read-after-read, no race window);<<db>>

if (Did the claim return a task?) then (no PENDING task available)
  :Nothing to do this cycle — return nil;
else (yes — task claimed & marked PROCESSED)
  :Derive the day window:
  startOfDay = task.TargetDate
  endOfDay   = startOfDay + 24h;
  :**Idempotent Recompute** —
  COUNT(*) State WHERE
   JobType = TICK,
   InstrumentID = task.InstrumentID,
   Timestamp IN [startOfDay, endOfDay),
   Status = CONFIRMED
  (the ONLY status counted as "resolved");<<db>>
  :UPDATE the matching CANDLE State row
  (JobType=CANDLE, same instrument & day):
  SET ResolvedTickCount = actualCount,
      UpdatedAt = time.Now().UTC();<<db>>
  if (actualCount < 24 ?) then (yes — incomplete day)
    :Also SET Status = PENDING
    on that CANDLE row — prevents a
    stale/corrupt Candle aggregation
    after an upstream Tick demotion;
  else (== 24, day fully resolved)
    :Candle row remains eligible for
    aggregation (ResolvedTickCount = 24
    is exactly what 03-candles-regular.puml checks for);
  endif
  :**Conditional DELETE** of the SyncTask:
  WHERE id = task.ID AND status = 'PROCESSED';<<db>>
  note right
    ** Lost-Update mitigation **
    If, while steps 3-4 were running, a NEW
    TICK event re-upserted this same task back
    to PENDING (publish side), this DELETE's
    WHERE clause matches zero rows — so the
    task safely survives for reprocessing on
    the very next Sync cycle. No event is lost.
  end note
endif

:wg.Done() — join point
(Parent Handler releases LockIDSync);
stop

@enduml
